{"id":58395,"ord":81,"n_segments":204,"prev":58394,"next":58396,"doc":{"id":"68359","title":"68359_Zutty Singleton oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Zutty Singleton","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/68359/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68359"},"chapter":"Chicago and New York shows, 1925-33","title":"Sid Catlett recommends Zutty to the Selbys","category":"band_or_employer","summary":"The Selbys got Zutty through Sid Catlett, who could not take the job; they work out which band Catlett was with in New York at the time.","period":"1933","year_from":1933,"year_to":1933,"words":128,"start":[124,4],"end":[125,8],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=68359#s58395","tags":{"places":[{"name":"Chicago","focus":0,"type":"city"},{"name":"New York","focus":0,"type":"city"}],"venues":[{"name":"Savoy Ballroom","focus":0,"city":"New York"}],"bands":[{"name":"Sammy Stewart's band","focus":0,"leader":"Sammy Stewart"},{"name":"Elmer Snowden's band","focus":0,"leader":"Elmer Snowden"}]},"people":[{"name":"Sid Catlett","qid":"Q720654","n":5},{"name":"Sammy Stewart","qid":"Q23639470","n":2},{"name":"Arlene Selby","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Norman Selby","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Elmer Snowden","qid":"Q489602","n":1}],"story":{"theme":18,"theme_name":"Getting paid: wages, tips and leaving over money","community":39,"community_name":"Battling at the Savoy Ballroom","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":124,"b":4,"s":"MRS. SINGLETON","x":"I wonder how did Eileen and Norman Selby happen to get you?"},{"p":124,"b":5,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Through Sid Catlett"},{"p":124,"b":6,"s":"MRS. SINGLETON","x":"Oh!"},{"p":124,"b":7,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"They wanted Sid Catlett, but Sid couldn't go because he had another job."},{"p":124,"b":8,"s":"MRS. SINGLETON","x":"Oh yes."},{"p":125,"b":0,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"So old Sid got me. Sid recommended me."},{"p":125,"b":1,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Well what was Sid, Who was Sid Cutlett (Cadley?) with at that time?"},{"p":125,"b":2,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"I think he was with Sammy Stewart."},{"p":125,"b":3,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Oh, in Chicago?"},{"p":125,"b":4,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"No, here."},{"p":125,"b":5,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Oh!"},{"p":125,"b":6,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"Here in New York."},{"p":125,"b":7,"s":"MR. DANCE","x":"Because he was with Elmer Snowden here at one time wasn't he? Elmer Snowden had a big band that was (Small?) something."},{"p":125,"b":8,"s":"MR. SINGLETON","x":"That maybe so. But I know he couldn't take the job because he had something else to do. So I don't know if that was the time he was with Sammy Stewart at the Savoy or what."}]}